{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["And he who eats from its carcass — the Sages explained: this is a measure, so that if one carries the volume of eating or touches, he is impure. And this is a ke-zayit. And according to the plain sense: one who eats is impure even though he did not touch it with his hands, as written: נבלה וטריפה לא יאכל לטמאה בה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:40.703464920Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}